WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.460
<i>Can't you see that you are sweet?</i>

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:15.050
<i>Oh, let me love you so.</i>

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.460
War in the Pocket

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>miageru sora wa tooi kedo</i>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>As I look up, the sky above seems so far away...</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>kakae kirenai yume ga aru</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>...but there are dreams that even it can't hold.</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>sou yo, tsukurareta sekai no naka wo mukidashite</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>Oh, yes, I want to slip away from this artificial world...</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>jiyuu ni naritai</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>...and make myself free.</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>hashi ni tsuzukete sora ni todoteba</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>I can keep on running till I finally reach the sky.</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>kaze ni nareru to sou shinjiteru kara</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>Since I can believe that I can become the wind someday...</i>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.450
<i>I never give up forever.</i>

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.540
They came back!

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.690
And at the End of the Rainbow?

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.700
<i>I wonder what's</i> <i>in this thing?</i>

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.700
<i>That's 38th street</i> <i>over there, so...</i>

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.570
It was a trailer with a big yellow-green container on it.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:08.150
It was headed towards Vera Cruz from Blue Plum Avenue.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.570
They were big ones, like they use in factories. Four, total.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.910
I want you guys to find it for me.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.920
It'll be easy for you cops to check out with your computers.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.080
Hey, are you listening?!

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.130
Yeah, I'm listening.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:27.050
I remember the license plate number: S-63 D-0018.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.880
Come on, listen to me!

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:34.010
Kid, quit playing detective. We're busy here!

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:38.140
Hold it! It was a hit and run!

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.150
I got hit here! And look over here, too!

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.570
This is car 16. En route towards Vera Cruz, sector 42.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.160
Will search for the hit and run suspect.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.280
<i>Roger.</i>

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.120
Now, kid, do you remember what the driver looked like?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.990
Yes, sir, I remember!

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:02.040
S-63 D-0018...
That's the number, all right.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.840
Kid, you're sure this is the car?

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.800
Yes, sir, that's it all right.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:13.390
Little bit to the left! All right! All right!

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.860
<i>Can I help you?</i>

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.020
<i>This is the police. We'd like</i> <i>to ask you some questions.</i>

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.490
I see. We'll open the shutter.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.150
Hold on a sec.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.540
Who's in charge here?

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:47.800
That'd be me, sir. What's the problem?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.300
That trailer out there... Is it yours?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:55.850
Well?!

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.180
We're renting it, but...

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.270
Mind if ask a couple more questions?

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.110
Kid, come over here.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.690
Is the man who hit you in here?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.280
Hit him? Hold on here! There must be some mistake!

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.910
I didn't ask you! Well, kid? Any of them familiar?

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.780
Hmmm...

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.660
That guy! That's the one who hit me!

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.540
Goddamn little!

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.790
Where were you this morning at 6:00?

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.460
I was in a trailer heading here from the space port.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.420
Which route did you take?

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:36.470
Blue Plum Avenue, through 38th Street.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.720
I see... Just like the kid says.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:43.310
Oh, come on! The little snot's lying!

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:46.060
You guys are acting awfully suspicious...

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.310
Like you're hiding something!

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:51.320
I'm getting real interested in what you've got in those containers.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.780
Let me see them.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.450
Foreman! Where's the open switch on this thing?

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:59.740
Could you open this thing up?

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:04.160
Oh, I'll get that for you. You need a keycard for it.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.160
Hurry up!

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.170
Uh, the card, the card...

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.680
Big brother!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.260
Kid, what's wrong?

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.310
Big brother, don't you remember me?

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:26.310
Al! Al, it's you! You've gotten so big!

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:32.940
I'm sorry, officer. I made up the story about the hit and run.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.490
I haven't seen my brother since my parents split up.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:42.620
I haven't seen him in four years, so when I saw him in the trailer...

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:47.370
...I lied so you'd look for him. I got bruised falling down.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.330
They don't have anything to do with a hit and run! I'm sorry!

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.630
Is this true?

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:54.170
Yes, sir... Al, shame on you!

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.800
You know it's wrong to lie to policemen.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.680
I'm sorry, big brother.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:02.390
Damn you! Bringing the cops here... Are you nuts?!

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.430
I wanted to know where you were!

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:06.310
And now that you do?

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:08.600
I want to join your group!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:12.230
Join our?! We're not playing war here!

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.480
Not play!

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.530
Captain, what do we do with this kid?

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:22.280
Your name is Alfred, right?

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:25.750
You're the captain, right? Please let me be in the team.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.120
Let me be a Zeon soldier. I've always wanted to be a soldier!

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:32.500
All right, but with a couple of conditions.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:33.670
Conditions?

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:37.630
Uh-huh. First, you can't tell anybody that we're here.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.260
I promise! I won't tell anyone!

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.600
And one more thing. I want to ask you about that video you shot.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:48.850
The container was here, in gate #8.

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:52.100
They probably took it down to block #12.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.520
Oh? What makes you say that?

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:58.820
Because they usually use lift C from gate #8...

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:00.660
...and that one goes down to block #12.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.620
You're a smart little kid, Al!

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.990
What was it carrying?

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.000
Our mission is to find that out.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.370
I'll help!

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.340
You've done enough for today.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:22.760
Thanks for your help. I'd like you to have this.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:29.730
It's our unit insignia. Don't lose it.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.650
If anyone asks, just tell them you found it.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.570
Aye, aye, Captain!

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.570
Bernie says he'll drive you home.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:47.370
What, you've never been in a car before?

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.450
Not with a pilot for a driver!

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.960
Gee, I'm flattered.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.090
I'll have Bernie keep an eye on him.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:05.340
I still say we shoulda killed him, or at least kept him here.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:08.260
There's no telling when that kid'll spill the beans!

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:11.100
You want to start a kidnapping investigation?

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:15.270
Well, at least this'll keep Bernie out of our hair.

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:16.900
Exactly.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.490
Getting killed in space is the worst.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.820
There's no gravity, and the blood just forms these huge globs...

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:30.750
...that float around the cockpit. It's worse than hell!

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.710
I've seen more of my buddies die than I can count.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:42.720
I really shouldn't even be associating with a kid like you.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.890
Bernie, have you ever killed anyone?

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:50.350
I don't want to kill them...

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.810
...but if I don't get them first, they'll get me.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.730
You have to take out your target, right?

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.690
Sounds rough...

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.230
You bet!

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:01.400
I was just one kill away from becoming an ace when they got me.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.280
Was the other pilot really good?

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:06.610
No, I was careless. They told us this was a neutral colony.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.080
The GMs just popped out, and... Well, what could I do?

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.580
Oh! Here! Turn right!

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.060
Al, I don't care if you had the day off today.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.770
You should tell me when you go out!

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:37.940
Yes, Mom.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:39.980
I got a letter from school today.

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:42.610
They want to talk with me about your grades!

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:45.570
You did really badly on your tests, didn't you?!

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:49.570
<i>Why didn't you tell me?</i> <i>Al, if you want to play...</i>

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:53.450
<i>...you have to earn it through</i> <i>good work. Understand?</i>

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:54.290
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.090
Al?

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.010
Yeah?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.930
I'm going to the women's association meeting.

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:15.680
Now, make sure you do all your homework!

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.100
Yes, Mom!

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.240
X minus Y equals...

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:36.290
Dad! Mom! Call the cops!

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:39.250
A prowler! I just caught a prowler out here!

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.010
Bernie...

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:55.310
Al, this creep was trying to sneak into your house!

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.850
That's my brother!

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:02.650
Brother?! Your brother...

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:11.030
Mom! Cancel the phone call!

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.620
Thank goodness. He's still alive.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:49.690
I'm really sorry about the misunderstanding.

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:52.450
Is coffee all right with you?

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:54.200
Sure...

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:04.080
So, you're Al's brother. I had no idea.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.250
We have different mothers.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:12.090
Dad was really young when I was born...

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:15.260
...and a lot of people objected to the marriage, so they separated.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.760
Does Michiko know about you?

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:21.100
It's a secret! That's why he was sneaking over.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:25.730
And so Chris here mistook him for a prowler.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:31.030
Forgive her. She just jumped to conclusions.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.700
Sure...

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:35.820
I'm really sorry. I just thought...

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:37.530
No harm done!

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:41.000
She's a real hot-head.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.290
Probably why she joined the Federal Forces!

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:47.790
Chris, you're a soldier?!

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.800
I just do data collection.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:52.260
It's not like I fight with a gun or anything.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:54.840
Bernie's a <i>real</i> soldier!

00:13:56.760 --> 00:14:00.890
No, I was discharged. I'm in the reserves now.

00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:05.140
So, that's why you came back to the colony. You also work here?

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.900
I work in a factory now. Mechanical stuff.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:15.820
Thanks for everything.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:19.200
You really should take it easy for a while...

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.120
I have to meet someone now.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.710
You're sure your head's all right?

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.620
It's fine, really.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:29.500
Uh, here. Thanks.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.380
Al, let's go.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:34.050
Goodnight, Chris.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.760
Goodnight.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:47.480
You can't judge people from how they look.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:49.610
I don't think she's bad...

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.360
Ow!

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:53.650
Does it hurt?

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.990
Just kidding... LAUNCH!

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:04.870
Bye, Mom!

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:12.920
Hey, Al!

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.920
We were on our way over!

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:16.840
Let's go to the park and play war!

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:21.550
Maybe next time! I'm busy today!

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.570
Secure those screens!

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:43.120
Which do we start with?

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.450
The main one!

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:45.700
Aye, sir.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:50.040
So, it was a mobile suit they had inside...

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:01.090
Bernie! Hurry up and lock it down!

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.430
Aye, sir!

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:07.430
Are you gonna fight the Feds with this?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:11.020
No, it's just for when we get off of this colony.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:14.610
You're not gonna fight, just run away?

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:18.320
Well, if the Feddies attack us, that'll be another thing.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:21.320
Then you should let Bernie be the pilot!

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:24.030
All he needs is one more kill to become an ace!

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:27.290
I'm sorry, but I've already chosen Misha to be the pilot.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:29.830
What's wrong with Bernie?

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:33.080
Misha just has more combat experience.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.500
Bernie! I'm so sorry!

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:38.760
Only one more kill 'til you're an ace, huh?

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.670
You only have four under your belt?

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:44.640
I figured Bernie would've gotten at least twenty by now!

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:11.250
<i>Chris, uh, let's</i> <i>take a break here.</i>

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.920
We'll try again in the afternoon with a new program.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.210
<i>Aye, sir.</i>

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.960
How's the reaction speed data reading?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.050
Her average has increased by 30%.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:22.260
We've got a long way to go to get it to 80%.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:27.390
So, what's your impression of the Alex?

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:31.140
How do you like the 360 degree monitor and the magnetic coating?

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:33.020
It's so fast, it's scary.

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:35.480
Can anyone really handle something this sensitive in combat?

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:38.730
Depends on the pilot, I suppose.

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:41.690
Oh, so you think I'm not good enough for the Alex?!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.990
Simmer down. This thing's specially built for Newtypes.

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:48.410
You're pretty good, but I think this is a little out of your class.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.990
You'd have to be some kind of a freak to control this thing.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.540
I hear they'll be sending it over to that pilot on <i>White Base.</i>

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:49.930
Al, let's call it a day.

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:53.680
We aren't going to find that secret Feddie base.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:56.270
The captain gave us a mission, right?

00:18:58.060 --> 00:18:59.100
I suppose.

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:05.690
Bernie, why would the Federation have to hide its base?

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:09.910
Because the security treaty between Side 6 and the Federation...

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:12.330
...isn't officially in effect yet.

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:18.750
In other words, there are still limits to what they can do here.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:26.170
I'm surprised there're so few cars with Fed license plates.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:33.390
If we find the base, do you think the captain'll change his mind?

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:35.640
Change his mind about what?

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:37.310
About you being the pilot.

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:40.190
Maybe he'll let you fly the mobile suit, instead of Misha.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.440
I'm not worried about who's going to be the pilot.

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:47.110
I'll get my chance to be an ace some other time.

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:54.330
Come on, Al, let's go. We'll get something to eat.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:55.950
Just a little longer...

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.840
Al, what happened? Hey!

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:13.350
We found it! We found it, Bernie!

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:20.520
Just because it was the same guy doesn't mean it's a Feddie base.

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:23.110
Why don't we get closer and check it out?

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:24.400
How?

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.650
Underground!

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:26.610
Underground?

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:29.690
We'll use the Colony Corporation's service tunnels.

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:39.370
All right!

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:51.430
If this is 2-27, then it should be about 200 meters up.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.970
Looks like this is gonna be pretty easy.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:59.310
Bernie, hurry up!

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:00.770
Calm down.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:02.480
Isn't it around here?

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:04.400
Should be a little further up.

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:06.480
Aw, it's blocked.

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:10.570
Can you unlock it?

00:21:10.610 --> 00:21:13.910
That's funny, I don't see a switch.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:16.870
Let's try it from the west side.

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:18.030
Okay!

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:24.920
I've got it!

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:26.250
What?

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:30.380
This block's the only one with new shutters installed.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:33.010
Meaning they have something in there now they don't want anyone to see.

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.840
They've got the container in there!

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:37.390
Bingo.

00:21:41.310 --> 00:21:42.520
Cheer up!

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:45.730
But we've got the base right here in front of us.

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:48.900
We did more than enough by just finding it.

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:52.070
Even if it's just a coincidence, this is a major break.

00:21:52.150 --> 00:21:54.400
The captain's gonna love this.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:58.990
Al! What're you up to?

00:22:16.510 --> 00:22:18.390
Forget it, Al! It's too dangerous!

00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:19.300
No way!

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:20.720
You could get killed!

00:22:20.890 --> 00:22:22.100
I'm fine!

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:32.730
Were you fine just now?

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:36.280
No problem. You're the one acting scared, Bernie.

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:40.330
I'll bet you're just a big coward when you're not in a mobile suit.

00:22:42.410 --> 00:22:44.410
Okay, our target is that projection over there.

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:47.120
Once I'm there, you come across on the wire.

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:48.330
Got it?

00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:49.630
Gotcha.

00:23:13.570 --> 00:23:15.940
It's all right. Coast is clear.

00:23:17.650 --> 00:23:19.450
Take off your spacesuit and hand it down to me.

00:23:19.490 --> 00:23:20.780
Okay.

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:32.040
<i>That sounds like machinery...</i>

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:36.970
Al! No!

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:43.050
Al, no! You'll get caught!

00:23:50.230 --> 00:23:52.270
The hours on this job really suck.

00:23:52.310 --> 00:23:55.280
I hope we get overtime for this!

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:57.530
Quit complaining.

00:23:57.860 --> 00:24:00.030
<i>Feddie soldiers!</i>

00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:26.400
<i>On that night I told them that lie...</i>

00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:26.400
<i>uso wo tsuita yoru ni wa</i>

00:25:26.990 --> 00:25:33.130
<i>...I couldn't sleep. That's how scared I was.</i>

00:25:26.990 --> 00:25:33.130
<i>nemurezu ni kowakatta</i>

00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:39.540
<i>But no matter how bad of a fight we would have...</i>

00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:39.540
<i>donna kenka wo shite mo</i>

00:25:39.840 --> 00:25:46.410
<i>...by the next day, it would be forgotten.</i>

00:25:39.840 --> 00:25:46.410
<i>tsugi no hi wa wasureteita</i>

00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:53.890
<i>The sky would be so blue...</i>

00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:53.890
<i>sora ga aoi koto</i>

00:25:54.740 --> 00:26:01.380
<i>...and that would make me so glad.</i>

00:25:54.740 --> 00:26:01.380
<i>sore ga ureshikute</i>

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:07.740
<i>There would be times when I'd doubt others...</i>

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:07.740
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:14.680
<i>...and I'd know the loneliness of living.</i>

00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:14.680
<i>ikiru sabishisa shiru koto mo</i>

00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:20.740
<i>But that was something I didn't notice then.</i>

00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:20.740
<i>ki ga tsukazu ni subete wo</i>

00:26:21.140 --> 00:26:26.180
<i>Back when I believed in everything...</i>

00:26:21.140 --> 00:26:26.180
<i>shinjiteta koro</i>

00:26:49.870 --> 00:26:51.380
NEXT EPISODE

00:26:51.650 --> 00:26:53.530
We're going to lose.

00:26:58.200 --> 00:26:59.700
What about the Alex?!

00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:01.410
Miss Mackenzie!

00:27:03.040 --> 00:27:03.830
Umm...

00:27:07.670 --> 00:27:09.170
The Zeon are the bad guys.

00:27:12.590 --> 00:27:14.380
Can you beat it, Bernie?

00:27:15.440 --> 00:27:17.440
WAR IN THE POCKET

00:27:17.440 --> 00:27:19.860
Episode 4 Over the River and Through the Woods
